{
  "schema_version": "report-evidence/1",
  "source_sha256": "457922d41ee5ef11e7ae11d61c4a22ccfa4258d3c1e4065265c08f838ae8b71c",
  "fragments": [
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0001",
      "text": "Epoch-boundary lock inclusion backdates ve-balance into prior epoch, enabling over-claim and reclaim underflow",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 110,
      "line": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0002",
      "text": "## Finding description and impact",
      "start": 112,
      "end": 145,
      "line": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0003",
      "text": "### Summary",
      "start": 147,
      "end": 158,
      "line": 5
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0004",
      "text": "`TrustBonding` computes prior-epoch rewards using epoch-end snapshots at `epochTimestampEnd(epoch)`, while `VotingEscrow` snapshot lookup is inclusive (`<= timestamp`).",
      "start": 159,
      "end": 327,
      "line": 6
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0005",
      "text": "Because of this, a lock action performed exactly at epoch boundary can be counted into the previous epoch entitlement window.",
      "start": 328,
      "end": 453,
      "line": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0006",
      "text": "The claim path then adds user rewards into `totalClaimedRewardsForEpoch[prevEpoch]` without an epoch-cap guard, allowing `totalClaimedRewardsForEpoch(epoch)` to exceed epoch emissions.",
      "start": 455,
      "end": 639,
      "line": 9
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0007",
      "text": "When reclaim logic computes unclaimed as `epochRewards - claimedRewards`, epochs with over-claimed totals underflow and revert.",
      "start": 641,
      "end": 768,
      "line": 11
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0008",
      "text": "### Root cause details",
      "start": 770,
      "end": 792,
      "line": 13
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0009",
      "text": "1. Inclusive prior-epoch balance reads:",
      "start": 794,
      "end": 833,
      "line": 15
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0010",
      "text": "- [`totalBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd` / `userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/314b7d4d9ccbaf27e4484a6c0706af83d3f75f36/src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol#L194-L213)",
      "start": 834,
      "end": 1045,
      "line": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0011",
      "text": "2. Eligibility uses those values:",
      "start": 1047,
      "end": 1080,
      "line": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0012",
      "text": "- [`_userEligibleRewardsForEpoch`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/314b7d4d9ccbaf27e4484a6c0706af83d3f75f36/src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol#L475-L491)",
      "start": 1081,
      "end": 1260,
      "line": 19
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0013",
      "text": "3. No epoch-cap in claim aggregate accounting:",
      "start": 1262,
      "end": 1308,
      "line": 21
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0014",
      "text": "- [`claimRewards` aggregate increment](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/314b7d4d9ccbaf27e4484a6c0706af83d3f75f36/src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol#L348-L387)",
      "start": 1309,
      "end": 1492,
      "line": 22
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0015",
      "text": "4. Reclaim underflow point:",
      "start": 1494,
      "end": 1521,
      "line": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0016",
      "text": "- [`getUnclaimedRewardsForEpoch` subtraction](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/314b7d4d9ccbaf27e4484a6c0706af83d3f75f36/src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol#L320-L340)",
      "start": 1522,
      "end": 1712,
      "line": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0017",
      "text": "5. Inclusive timestamp lookup in ve snapshots:",
      "start": 1714,
      "end": 1760,
      "line": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0018",
      "text": "- [`_find_timestamp_epoch`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/314b7d4d9ccbaf27e4484a6c0706af83d3f75f36/src/external/curve/VotingEscrow.sol#L544-L576)",
      "start": 1761,
      "end": 1929,
      "line": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0019",
      "text": "- [`_find_user_timestamp_epoch` + `_balanceOf`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/314b7d4d9ccbaf27e4484a6c0706af83d3f75f36/src/external/curve/VotingEscrow.sol#L590-L638)",
      "start": 1930,
      "end": 2118,
      "line": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0020",
      "text": "### Impact",
      "start": 2120,
      "end": 2130,
      "line": 31
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0021",
      "text": "A boundary-time injector can claim prior-epoch rewards despite not being a genuine prior-epoch participant, causing over-distribution and reclaim failures.",
      "start": 2131,
      "end": 2286,
      "line": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0022",
      "text": "Observed PoC outputs:",
      "start": 2288,
      "end": 2309,
      "line": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0023",
      "text": "- `epoch1_emissions = 1000000000000000000000`",
      "start": 2310,
      "end": 2355,
      "line": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0024",
      "text": "- `first_claim = 1000000000000000000000`",
      "start": 2356,
      "end": 2396,
      "line": 36
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0025",
      "text": "- `second_claim = 999666777562686266743`",
      "start": 2397,
      "end": 2437,
      "line": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0026",
      "text": "- `total_claimed = 1999666777562686266743`",
      "start": 2438,
      "end": 2480,
      "line": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0027",
      "text": "- `excess_bps = 9996`",
      "start": 2481,
      "end": 2502,
      "line": 39
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0028",
      "text": "Boundary sensitivity:",
      "start": 2504,
      "end": 2525,
      "line": 41
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0029",
      "text": "- `offset 0` gives positive retroactive claimable.",
      "start": 2526,
      "end": 2576,
      "line": 42
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0030",
      "text": "- `offset +1s` gives `0` retroactive claimable.",
      "start": 2577,
      "end": 2624,
      "line": 43
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0031",
      "text": "Severity rationale:",
      "start": 2626,
      "end": 2645,
      "line": 45
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0032",
      "text": "- Impact is material once triggered (over-claim + reclaim DoS on affected epoch).",
      "start": 2646,
      "end": 2727,
      "line": 46
    },
    {
      "id": "e_457922d41ee5_0033",
      "text": "- Exploitability is constrained by exact boundary timing (`offset == 0`), so Medium is appropriate.",
      "start": 2728,
      "end": 2827,
      "line": 47
    }
  ]
}
